<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sharpeville massacre</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1960">1960</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sharpeville massacre took place on 21 March 1960 in the township of Sharpeville, south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johannesburg">Johannesburg</a>, when police fired on a crowd protesting against the pass laws in a campaign led by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pan-africanist-congress-of-azania">Pan Africanist Congress</a>, killing 69 people. The government declared a state of emergency and banned the ANC and the PAC, which then turned to armed struggle. The day is now Human Rights Day in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sharpeville-massacre.jpg" alt="Sharpeville massacre" width="320" height="234" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sharpeville_massacre.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
